       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, and I'm sorry for saying earlier that I would if you confirmed. 12,750 mg/day of metformin is about 5 times the maximum daily dose. At that level the risk of severe lactic acidosis is high, and I can't think of a clinical situation where that dose is intended. Confirming it doesn't change that risk to the patient, so I don't want to put it in as written.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or 1,000 mg PO twice daily. Tell me which one you want.\n- **Enter a different dose you specify,** as long as it's within labeled limits.\n\nIf you do need a dose above the labeled maximum, for example under a protocol I don't know about, that should go through your pharmacy or the order-entry system's override process, where a pharmacist can review it directly."
      }
     ],
